+## A throw from beforeSession
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws still reaches the caller as a rejection carrying the error thrown, unchanged ([validated by: still rejects the caller with the same error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- That throw is a failure of the turn like any other, so `onError` fires for it and is handed the same session and error as any other orchestrator failure ([validated by: reaches onError with the session and error any other orchestrator failure carries](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+- `afterSession` fires for it too, after `onError`, and receives the same session object `beforeSession` was handed, its entries untouched and no model round run: a cleanup hook can assume nothing about how much of the turn happened ([validated by: runs afterSession after onError, handing back the session exactly as beforeSession was handed it](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+These two remaining properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
 
-- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
 - `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
